Z||000000||Philphine||03-27-2001||12:25 PM||||<BR>i mentioned the amps i use in my '87 coupe when i first joined here. two soundstreams, an sf90 (4 channel 2x30 ad 2x15, about7"x7"x2.5") and a d60 (2 channel 3x30 bridged to 1x80, about 7"x3.5"x2.5") both pretty small amps the work well for me. long discontinued but worth looking for and/or picking up if you come across either.<P>yesterday i picked up another amp that should come in handy size and power output wise. a nacamichi pa102. very small 5"x3.5x1.5". 2x15 watts. should be just enough to power rear seat speakers. 15 watts may not sound like much compared to the advertised claims of most head units, but this is rms of a nice outboard amp compared to max specs of a typical head unit. it would also allow you to run out of your head unit into an eq or processor of choice to amp channels that are independent of what ever signal and power the front speakers are getting. good for letting front speakers (usually bigger) use more powerful amp channels, being able to keep fading, time delay setups or using a different crossover point. <P>unfortunatly, this is an older amp also but still something consider if you come across it.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
